mote repositiories, WORKSPACE file."},{"id":1197679449,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMTk3Njc5NDQ5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/labels/bad%20error%20messaging","name":"bad error messaging","color":"e07d80","default":false,"description":"Issues where users get stuck because they don't understand what they did wrong"}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2019-02-01T11:59:27Z","updated_at":"2021-11-29T13:19:29Z","closed_at":"2019-02-15T09:24:51Z","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Typically, if I want to use a github project/library, I navigate to github page of that project and copy the url of the released contents, typically an archive.\r\nAt this moment, I am not aware of the prefix that is used inside the archive, it for sure is combined name and version, but it can use minuses (-) or underscores (_) or \"v\" symbol for the version.\r\n\r\nIt would be nice of the error about the wrong prefix informed me which prefix it actually was.\r\n\r\nFor instance, instead of:\r\nERROR: <...>/3ef9cfc3a9b14f5d67990ffd01552d35/external/rules_foreign_cc_tests/configure_gnuplot/BUILD:4:1: no such package '@zlib//': java.io.IOException: Prefix zlib-1.2.111 was given, but not found in the archive and referenced by '@rules_foreign_cc_tests//configure_gnuplot:libz'\r\nERROR: Analysis of target '@rules_foreign_cc_tests//configure_gnuplot:test_zlib' failed; build aborted: Analysis failed\r\n\r\nIt could say \"Prefix XYZ was given, the actual prefix is ZYX\"","closed_by":{"login":"bazel-io","id":15028808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io","html_url":"https://github